**who —** THE HUMAN — a techne sphere — the art

**what —** Halfway up the ladder, in scale as much as in spirit, is the human — the one rung that looks at all the others. A person is about as many times larger than a cell as a galaxy is larger than a person; we sit, astonishingly, near the geometric middle of everything there is. The art renders that with the oldest geometry of the body: the Vitruvian figure in circle and square.

